data gunbc_host_converge_receipt_grammar_marker: String = "BYTE-EXACT converge-receipt wire contract (FROZEN v1 with fierce-carp-462, 2026-06-24; EMIT is the single authority, the ctrl reconciler aligns to THIS with no fallback, mirroring gunbc_runner_deploy_manifest_contract_marker). Three line-kinds, KV-by-name, order-independent, unknown-KV ignored forward-compatibly: (1) PER-KNOB -- converge-receipt host=<id> slice=<runner|sessions> knob=<name> desired=<val> effective=<val> verdict=<converged|drifted|absent> -- emitted after the .sh applies+reads-back ONE knob. (2) SUMMARY -- converge-receipt host=<id> applied=<int> drifted=<int> verdict=<converged|drifted|absent> -- one per host after its knobs. (3) SESSIONS-MEMBERSHIP -- converge-receipt host=<id> slice=sessions sessions_in_slice=<int> sessions_legacy_flat=<int> verdict=<converged|absent> -- one per managed-sessions host; the COUNTS feed stern-dove-499's OomdEnforced membership conjunct (gunbc PR #5726): sessions_in_slice = docker-*.scope parented under sessions.slice (the guard keys on > 0; an EMPTY slice has no cgroup dir, which emits sessions_in_slice=0 NOT absent/error), sessions_legacy_flat = docker-*.scope still under system.slice (diagnostic-only, distinguishes all-legacy from empty-host). verdict=absent before ctrl #1804 populates the slice is EXPECTED and HOLDs. Line-kind discriminator: knob= present => per-knob; applied= present => summary; sessions_in_slice= present => sessions-membership. SEMANTICS mapped to std.realization_reconcile.Reconciliation (see converge_verdict): verdict=converged => Converged(evidence); verdict=drifted AND verdict=absent BOTH => NotConverged(reason) (absent = the ReadAbsent read-presence gate, expected early e.g. sessions.slice before it is populated). ctrl HOLDs a host unless its summary verdict=converged AND every per-knob line for that host is verdict=converged (defense-in-depth: a converged summary with any drifted/absent knob still HOLDs). The knob set is the FOLD of cpu_weight + build_tokens + the memory caps + runner width: slice=runner -- runner_slice_cap_bytes, per_slot_memory_max_bytes, cpu_weight, build_tokens, runner_count; slice=sessions -- slice_max_bytes, per_session_max_bytes, oom_pressure_kill, oom_pressure_limit_pct, cpu_weight."

data gunbc_cgroup_v2_root: String = "/sys/fs/cgroup"
data gunbc_sessions_legacy_parent_slice: String = "system.slice"

data gunbc_runner_unit_template: String = "actions-runner@.service"
data gunbc_runner_per_slot_dropin_path: String = "/etc/systemd/system/actions-runner@.service.d/20-fleet-width.conf"
data gunbc_runner_jobserver_env_file: String = "/etc/default/ctrl-jobserver"
data gunbc_runner_jobserver_env_key: String = "CTRL_JOBSERVER_TOKENS"
data gunbc_runner_jobserver_service: String = "ctrl-jobserver.service"

data gunbc_host_converge_grounded_mechanism_marker: String = "The apply/read mechanisms are GROUNDED (signed by fierce-carp-462 2026-06-24, read out of the retiring deploy-runner-fleet-width.sh / deploy-session-slice.sh, NOT guessed): runner per-slot SERVICE template = actions-runner@.service, per-host instance glob = actions-runner@<host>-*.service; runner SLICE = system-actions-runner.slice (the implicit slice of the template, set-property MemoryMax/CPUWeight LIVE); per-slot cap = template drop-in 20-fleet-width.conf ([Service] MemoryMax) + daemon-reload (future instances) PLUS set-property on each active instance (effective NOW -- the drop-in-alone is the inert-cap trap this closes); WIDTH decrease = drain-before-stop (systemctl stop = SIGTERM to Runner.Listener which finishes the in-flight job; never SIGKILL) then disable, highest-NN-first; ordering invariant caps-before-widen (runner_count is the LAST runner knob); build_tokens = /etc/default/ctrl-jobserver CTRL_JOBSERVER_TOKENS=<int> + restart ctrl-jobserver.service (FIFO-safe shrink by attrition). SAFETY-CRITICAL: per_session_max_bytes is CARRY+VERIFY ONLY -- the converge NEVER set-property's it and NEVER enumerate-and-caps existing session scopes (the spawn path, ctrl #1804 docker --memory, owns the per-container write); the reconciler only SAMPLES a child .scope MemoryMax for read-back."

type ConvergeVerdict
  = Converged
  | Drifted
  | Absent


fn converge_verdict(effective: String, expected: String) -> ConvergeVerdict {
  if effective == "" { Absent }
  else { if effective == expected { Converged } else { Drifted } }
}

fn converge_verdict_label(v: ConvergeVerdict) -> String {
  match v {
    Converged => "converged"
    Drifted => "drifted"
    Absent => "absent"
  }
}

type ConvergeSlice
  = RunnerSlice
  | SessionsSlice

fn converge_slice_label(s: ConvergeSlice) -> String {
  match s {
    RunnerSlice => "runner"
    SessionsSlice => "sessions"
  }
}

type ConvergeTarget
  = SliceProperty { unit: String, property: String, apply_value: String, expected_effective: String }
  | PerSlotMemoryCap { dropin_path: String, instance_glob: String, property: String, bytes_value: String }
  | RunnerWidth { instance_glob: String }
  | JobserverTokens { env_file: String, env_key: String, service_unit: String }
  | VerifyOnlyCap { slice_unit: String, property: String }

type ConvergeKnob {
  slice: ConvergeSlice
  name: String
  desired: String
  target: ConvergeTarget
}

data gunbc_host_converge_runner_sessions_coupling_marker: String = "DECISION (wise-eagle-664 model authority + fierce-carp-462 consumer + sharp-heron-321 plan, 2026-06-24; SHIP v1-coupled, SPLIT is the named end-state): host_converge_of folds ALL knobs + the sessions-membership probe into ONE HostConverge with ONE host_summary per host. The §4 de-conflation the end-state wants: a host has THREE INDEPENDENTLY-GROUNDED converge targets that should fingerprint-settle independently -- (T1) sessions.slice CAPS (slice_max / per_session / ManagedOOM kill+limit / cpu_weight), the UNGATED bootstrap (#5706), settleable as soon as set-property+verify-effective succeed; (T2) sessions MEMBERSHIP (sessions_in_slice>0), genuinely gated on ctrl #1804 populating the slice; (T3) runner COUNT+CAPS+width, gated on the full sound plan (RunnerSlotEnforced + OomdEnforced). Folding all three into one host_summary means the T2 membership HOLD blocks the already-settleable T1/T3 from fingerprint-settling, so ctrl re-runs the full privileged converge each pass (re-applying the runner-width 12->7) until #1804 lands. SHIP v1-coupled because: (a) it is SAFE and SAFE-BY-the-right-reason, not just expedient -- decoupling membership from the host verdict WITHOUT splitting the fingerprint would be FAIL-OPEN (the host would fingerprint converged while sessions.slice has no members for oomd to evict = zero actual protection, the §5 fail-open fierce-carp's defense-in-depth guards); (b) every apply is idempotent so the re-runs are harmless; (c) the runner-width decrease DOES apply each pass and we WANT it; (d) the bite-window (runner-plan-SOUND AND pre-#1804) does not exist yet (runner plan is RunnerSlotUnenforced today). ALTERNATIVE = the SPLIT end-state (split the host fingerprint by grounding-target T1/T2/T3 -- separate per-(host,target) HostConverge entries or per-target fingerprints -- so T1/T3 settle while only the genuinely-blocked T2/oomd part HOLDs, KEEPING the membership gate on the sessions-protection verdict so it stays fail-closed). This REQUIRES a receipt-grammar v2 (the SUMMARY line gains a grounding-target discriminator and the ctrl converged-decision keys on (host,target) not host) + re-coordination with fierce-carp's frozen v1 parser + 22 tests. dissolve-on: when the runner-sound-AND-pre-#1804 window becomes real and long enough that the redundant privileged re-runs matter (or sooner if a per-target settled receipt is wanted for observability), do the T1/T2/T3 fingerprint split + bump the receipt grammar to v2, co-designed with fierce-carp."

type SessionsMembershipProbe
  = MembershipProbe { slice_cgroup: String, legacy_cgroup: String }
  | NoMembershipProbe

type HostConverge {
  identity: HostIdentity
  knobs: List<ConvergeKnob>
  membership: SessionsMembershipProbe
}

type ConvergePolicy
  = ConvergePolicyDerived { hosts: List<HostConverge> }
  | ConvergePolicyUnsound { reason: String }

fn runner_instance_glob(host: HostIdentity) -> String {
  concat(concat("actions-runner@", host), "-*.service")
}

fn slice_numeric_knob(slice: ConvergeSlice, name: String, unit: String, property: String, value: Int) -> ConvergeKnob {
  let v = to_string(value)
  ConvergeKnob {
    slice: slice,
    name: name,
    desired: v,
    target: SliceProperty { unit: unit, property: property, apply_value: v, expected_effective: v },
  }
}

fn runner_host_knobs(h: RunnerHostDeployment) -> List<ConvergeKnob> {
  let glob = runner_instance_glob(host: h.identity)
  [
    slice_numeric_knob(
      slice: RunnerSlice,
      name: "runner_slice_cap_bytes",
      unit: gunbc_runner_slot_unit_placeholder,
      property: systemd_memory_max_property,
      value: byte_size_count(b: h.runner_slice_cap)
    ),
    ConvergeKnob {
      slice: RunnerSlice,
      name: "per_slot_memory_max_bytes",
      desired: to_string(byte_size_count(b: h.per_runner_memory_cap)),
      target: PerSlotMemoryCap {
        dropin_path: gunbc_runner_per_slot_dropin_path,
        instance_glob: glob,
        property: systemd_memory_max_property,
        bytes_value: to_string(byte_size_count(b: h.per_runner_memory_cap)),
      },
    },
    slice_numeric_knob(
      slice: RunnerSlice,
      name: "cpu_weight",
      unit: gunbc_runner_slot_unit_placeholder,
      property: systemd_cpu_weight_property,
      value: workload_class_cpu_weight(wc: h.workload_class)
    ),
    ConvergeKnob {
      slice: RunnerSlice,
      name: "build_tokens",
      desired: to_string(hardware_thread_count_value(t: h.build_tokens)),
      target: JobserverTokens {
        env_file: gunbc_runner_jobserver_env_file,
        env_key: gunbc_runner_jobserver_env_key,
        service_unit: gunbc_runner_jobserver_service,
      },
    },
    ConvergeKnob {
      slice: RunnerSlice,
      name: "runner_count",
      desired: to_string(h.runner_count),
      target: RunnerWidth { instance_glob: glob },
    },
  ]
}

fn session_host_knobs(slice_max: ByteSize, per_session: ByteSize) -> List<ConvergeKnob> {
  let kill_value = managed_oom_action_value(a: gunbc_oomd_sessions_policy.managed_oom_memory_pressure)
  let pct = to_string(percent_count(p: gunbc_oomd_sessions_policy.managed_oom_memory_pressure_limit))
  [
    slice_numeric_knob(
      slice: SessionsSlice,
      name: "slice_max_bytes",
      unit: gunbc_oomd_sessions_slice,
      property: systemd_memory_max_property,
      value: byte_size_count(b: slice_max)
    ),
    ConvergeKnob {
      slice: SessionsSlice,
      name: "per_session_max_bytes",
      desired: to_string(byte_size_count(b: per_session)),
      target: VerifyOnlyCap {
        slice_unit: gunbc_oomd_sessions_slice,
        property: systemd_memory_max_property,
      },
    },
    ConvergeKnob {
      slice: SessionsSlice,
      name: "oom_pressure_kill",
      desired: "true",
      target: SliceProperty {
        unit: gunbc_oomd_sessions_slice,
        property: oomd_managed_oom_memory_pressure_property,
        apply_value: kill_value,
        expected_effective: kill_value,
      },
    },
    ConvergeKnob {
      slice: SessionsSlice,
      name: "oom_pressure_limit_pct",
      desired: pct,
      target: SliceProperty {
        unit: gunbc_oomd_sessions_slice,
        property: oomd_managed_oom_memory_pressure_limit_property,
        apply_value: concat(pct, "%"),
        expected_effective: concat(pct, "%"),
      },
    },
    slice_numeric_knob(
      slice: SessionsSlice,
      name: "cpu_weight",
      unit: gunbc_oomd_sessions_slice,
      property: systemd_cpu_weight_property,
      value: workload_class_cpu_weight(wc: InteractiveLatencySensitive)
    ),
  ]
}

fn session_knobs_by_host(mode: SessionReservationMode) -> List<ConvergeKnob>? {
  match mode {
    SessionReservationModeUnset => none
    Regime1WorstCase { point: _ } => none
    Regime2AggregateOomd { oomd_eviction_ceiling: ceiling, session_concurrency: _, aggregate_reservation: agg } =>
      match agg {
        SessionAggregateUnmeasured => none
        SessionAggregateMeasured { bytes: agg_bytes } =>
          Present { value: session_host_knobs(
            slice_max: agg_bytes,
            per_session: ceiling
          ) }
      }
  }
}

fn sessions_membership_probe(session_knobs: List<ConvergeKnob>) -> SessionsMembershipProbe {
  if session_knobs.length() > 0 {
    MembershipProbe {
      slice_cgroup: concat(concat(gunbc_cgroup_v2_root, "/"), gunbc_oomd_sessions_slice),
      legacy_cgroup: concat(concat(gunbc_cgroup_v2_root, "/"), gunbc_sessions_legacy_parent_slice),
    }
  } else {
    NoMembershipProbe
  }
}

fn host_converge_of(h: RunnerHostDeployment, session_knobs: List<ConvergeKnob>) -> HostConverge {
  HostConverge {
    identity: h.identity,
    knobs: concat(runner_host_knobs(h: h), session_knobs),
    membership: sessions_membership_probe(session_knobs: session_knobs),
  }
}

fn fleet_converge_policy_from(plan: RunnerDeploymentPlan, mode: SessionReservationMode) -> ConvergePolicy {
  match plan {
    PlanUnsound { reason: reason } =>
      ConvergePolicyUnsound { reason: concat("runner deployment unsound: ", reason) }
    PlanDerived { hosts: hosts, fleet_concurrent_runs: _ } => {
      let session_knobs = match session_knobs_by_host(mode: mode) {
        Present { value: ks } => ks
        Absent => []
      }
      ConvergePolicyDerived {
        hosts: map(hosts, h => host_converge_of(h: h, session_knobs: session_knobs)),
      }
    }
  }
}

fn fleet_converge_policy() -> ConvergePolicy {
  fleet_converge_policy_from(plan: runner_deployment_plan(), mode: gunbc_ci_session_reservation_mode)
}
